title: Coalition Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: lwusp_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0 and in_usp_coalition = 0 and in_srp_majority = 0
card-image: img/portraits/rayne_cabinet.jpg
#subtitle: There is dissent within our coalition.

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. The other members of the coalition are constantly criticizing us for our policies, and are threatening to call a vote of no confidence to collapse this government.

How do we reduce tensions with the coalition?

- @promise_cuts: Agree to give our allies more credit for our shared success.
- @resources: Use our party resources to support our allies.
- @bring_down: Instead, we will bring down the government with a no-confidence vote, and call for new elections.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard



@promise_cuts
on-arrival: workers_lwusp -= 6; new_middle_lwusp -= 6; old_middle_lwusp -= 6; rural_lwusp -= 6; unemployed_lwusp -= 6; workers_cps += 6 if in_peoples_front_coalition; unemployed_cps += 6 if in_peoples_front_coalition; new_middle_cps += 6 if in_peoples_front_coalition; rural_cps += 6 if in_peoples_front_coalition; old_middle_cps += 6 if in_peoples_front_coalition; workers_pfjp += 6 if in_centrist_coalition; unemployed_pfjp += 6 if in_centrist_coalition; new_middle_pfjp += 6 if in_centrist_coalition; rural_pfjp += 6 if in_centrist_coalition; old_middle_pfjp += 6 if in_centrist_coalition; coalition_dissent -= 1

Fine. We have agreed to give our allies more credit for their extraordinary efforts in the shared rule of this country.

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: historical_mode = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2: We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: Bring down this government before our opponents do.
on-arrival: lwusp_in_government = 0; in_usp_coalition = 0; in_peoples_front_coalition = 0; in_centrist_coalition = 0; in_left_liberal_coalition = 0; in_left_usp_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Vacant"; chancellor_party = "Vacant"; vp_person = "Vacant"; vp_party = "Vacant"; president = "Vacant"; president_party = "Vacant"; pro_republic -= 5; new_middle_lwusp -= 3; rural_lwusp -= 3; old_middle_lwusp -= 3; workers_lwusp -= 3; unemployed_lwusp -= 3
go-to: elections

We have called for a vote of no confidence in ourselves, and have brought down this government.


@elections
call: set_next_election_time

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
